motivation: Nothing changes until you move. One small step is enough to begin.
discipline: Your habits are always watching. Make them proud when nobody else is looking.
money: True wealth is built in the quiet moments when you choose patience over applause.
mindset: My first thought is a draft, not the final version of this day.
fact: Some whales can live for over two centuries, carrying harpoons from the 1800s in their blubber.
books: Your mind runs on fast intuition and slow reasoning; pause to engage the slower system when stakes rise.
stoic: We are not short on time; we are careless with the hours we already have.
